#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f26d941b-b4b4-591e-b7e0-ae4bbf81e94b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With Two Independent Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af953589-81a6-5fe5-bfe1-3c3ff400edf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8st(s - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165128} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f181c1-2a8b-50c1-8b31-55133815ead5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8st(t - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165129} {:answer/id #uuid "3387fa45-98cf-5c2f-b848-179ecd225fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^{2}(2t - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165130} {:answer/id #uuid "47081aa9-15d2-59e4-93d0-374cdf5e8ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s^{2}(s - t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165131} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9b1ba3-49b1-5570-96f7-92cab4645579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s^{2}t(s - t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1f181c1-2a8b-50c1-8b31-55133815ead5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8st(t - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165129} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc879cca-6a9f-5bd8-9c28-f3961cc6728e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1e3cf4a-155f-587d-ba03-cc737759407e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94448" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-4y,$ where $x=2st$ and $y={s}^{2}t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(2st)=4st, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =2st.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(4st)(2t)+(-4)(2st) \\\\  & =8s{t}^{2}-8st \\\\  & =8st(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f26d941b-b4b4-591e-b7e0-ae4bbf81e94b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With Two Independent Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38252138-248d-5fc1-8988-a3ff2efa765a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t{e}^{st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337184} {:answer/id #uuid "2eaefb92-722a-5398-b368-816bb03c8e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337185} {:answer/id #uuid "15f476e0-2b06-5912-9ee4-083657a9e6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t({e}^{st}-{e}^{-st})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337186} {:answer/id #uuid "bf607762-cc10-5ab7-8db3-61ffc1f90228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337187} {:answer/id #uuid "99ecf009-aac0-5449-b33a-6e78ebbf08df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t({e}^{2st}+{e}^{-2st})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15f476e0-2b06-5912-9ee4-083657a9e6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t({e}^{st}-{e}^{-st})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337186} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f83934-c065-5d6e-b769-2db25e1663f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fdfd0b6-2c3b-50ac-bc5c-0d29eeafd8d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94747" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y},$ where $x={e}^{st}$ and $y={e}^{-st}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{1}{({e}^{st})^{2}}=-{e}^{-2st}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{1}{({e}^{-st})^{2}}=-{e}^{2st}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =t{e}^{st}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-t{e}^{-st}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(-{e}^{-2st})(t{e}^{st})+(-{e}^{2st})(-t{e}^{-st}) \\\\  & =t{e}^{st}-t{e}^{-st} \\\\  & =t({e}^{st}-{e}^{-st}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Function of Three Intermediate Variables and Two Independent Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4091250c-7695-5baf-ba82-311a7d20076d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "st{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359364} {:answer/id #uuid "2b89daae-b256-5c93-87cc-b28b654fad98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t+2){e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359365} {:answer/id #uuid "08658397-2af8-577b-be9d-b0c1d27357d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359366} {:answer/id #uuid "303ef2df-4798-5c6e-a1da-3514b057cdd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({t}^{2}-1){e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359367} {:answer/id #uuid "d245bd8d-566f-561b-a623-f8d7a5be3694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d245bd8d-566f-561b-a623-f8d7a5be3694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359368} :answer-field/id #uuid "73434767-a57d-5756-8581-c4b42bcddadf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a6b18b5-6eca-5bcb-8bc4-42eedbe5cf58" :question/math-academy-id "q-94813" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x+y+z},$ where $x=s-t,$ $y={t}^{2}$ and $z=s+t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{x+y+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x+y+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={e}^{x+y+z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =2t, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot (-1)+({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot 2t+({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}+2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}+{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167267 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Function of Three Intermediate Variables and Two Independent Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "916f71d9-1461-5cbc-a96a-fa2facdfc84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t + 4s - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165152} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf9c459-9ead-5506-8296-67e11bcaa57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t - 3s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165153} {:answer/id #uuid "cff4bcaf-76ab-55eb-8c51-2853168f6c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165154} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6ff427-9bf3-58ed-9f8f-8edd6d37b239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 - 8s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165155} {:answer/id #uuid "5998c176-c992-5217-8977-1683ab72fccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5998c176-c992-5217-8977-1683ab72fccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165156} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ab6d1c-5493-5461-9355-8385cc0e3f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db13dec0-b66e-50d3-9ee6-bdc2288dd174" :question/math-academy-id "q-94814" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=4x+3y-2z,$ where $x=2{s}^{2}-t,$ $y=s+3{t}^{2}$ and $z=4{s}^{2}+{t}^{2}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069068/assets/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =4s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =8s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(4)\\cdot 4s+(3)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 8s \\\\  & =16s+3-16s \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ca6dfb-d6af-559c-82bf-ebef070247b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359371} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7e3d5f-ce3f-53a2-8ca5-49d857f63430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359372} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a3ad7f-7674-54d8-8241-16b0a9d49b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359373} {:answer/id #uuid "9360bdf0-1ac6-5f4f-8bb4-9a6cd43a5b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359374} {:answer/id #uuid "440cc302-7062-5eb8-8252-a123c74e21eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ca6dfb-d6af-559c-82bf-ebef070247b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359371} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e425e93-f692-5345-8f23-5bdc03925a49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da628d4c-a325-5343-bcd6-7344b3c8f181" :question/math-academy-id "q-95114" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nAssume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDomain clarification: The problem assumes $x>0$, so $\\sqrt{x^2}=x$ in the source derivation above. Without that assumption, $f(x,x^3)=|x|\\sqrt{1+x^4}$ and\n$$\\frac{df}{dx}=\\operatorname{sgn}(x)\\frac{1+3x^4}{\\sqrt{1+x^4}}\\quad(x\\ne0).$$\nFor $x<0$ the derivative is the negative of the displayed answer. At $x=0$, the one-sided difference quotients tend to $-1$ and $1$, so the derivative does not exist. The original unqualified prompt and worked solution remain preserved in the source capture and database history."}]}
